1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
Hypertension is now Bangladesh's
most common illness,

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:14,500
yet only about one in ten people with it
has it under control.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Our grandparents collect medicines from a hospital doctor,
a village doctor and the local drug shop,

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:29,500
under thousands of brand names.
Nobody ever looks at the whole shelf.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
OushodhSathi is a pharmacist
for every elderly home.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
A family member photographs every medicine.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
We turn the pile into one doctor-checked list, in Bangla,

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:59,500
with a helper called Sathi,
and a medicine passport for every doctor visit.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
This is a demo household: Rahima Begum, 68.
Her daughter photographs the shelf,

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
and the list builds itself.

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,500
Here: Napa and Ace. Different names, same medicine:
paracetamol, twice.

12
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:16,000
Different names, same medicine:
so a pharmacist checks every one.

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:22,000
A pharmacist checks the evidence, with an AI summary
they must verify, and confirms it.

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Only then does the family see it, in simple Bangla.

15
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
The passport says what each medicine is for,

16
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
and its QR opens an emergency page:
no login, first name only.

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:44,000
For a mother who can't read,
today's medicines are pictures, read aloud.

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Blood pressure can be read
from a photo of the machine.

19
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Sathi, our helper, always shows the next step,

20
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:59,000
and when Nusrat asks "Should Ma stop Ace?", Sathi doesn't guess.
It sends the question to the pharmacist.

21
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Before every visit, one page shows what changed,
and who changed it.

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:15,000
AI does perception: a vision model reads cut strips and prescriptions,
and unknown brands must cite a source.

23
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Rules and humans do judgement: a deterministic engine checks every list,
and a clinician confirms every flag.

24
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:30,000
In our 80-question safety test, Sathi sent all 30 medical questions
to a pharmacist, and every emergency to 999.

25
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:40,000
It's built for parents who can't read,
and children far away.

26
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Families abroad pay; parents stay safe.

27
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,000
We are now recruiting our first pilot families,
and will publish results only when they are real.

28
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:58,000
OushodhSathi.
Build locally, protect globally.
